#: ../../source/developer-guide/documentation.md:133
msgid "Translations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/documentation.md:135
msgid ""
"The English Markdown pages are the only source. Translations are kept as "
"gettext `.po` files in `docs/source/locale/<language>/LC_MESSAGES/`, one per"
" page, each pairing an English string (`msgid`) with its translation "
"(`msgstr`). A string with an empty `msgstr` is shown in English, so a page "
"can be translated piece by piece."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/documentation.md:141
msgid "After changing English pages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/documentation.md:147
msgid ""
"New strings arrive untranslated; strings whose English changed are marked "
"`#, fuzzy` and shown in English until the translation is updated and the "
"`fuzzy` line removed. Then fill in `msgstr` and check with `make -C docs "
"live-zh`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/documentation.md:152
msgid ""
"Keep the Markdown syntax of the English string in the translation: inline "
"code, links (with the same targets) and emphasis. A link missing from a "
"translation fails the strict build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/documentation.md:156
msgid ""
"To add a language, add its code to `TRANSLATIONS` in `docs/Makefile`, a "
"build target like `html-zh`, and an entry in `site_languages` in "
"`_templates/header-links.html`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/documentation.md:160
msgid "C++ API pages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/developer-guide/documentation.md:162
msgid ""
"Doxygen extracts comments from `code/` (excluding the vendored `gzstream/`, "
"`lbfgsb/`, and `matexp/` directories) into XML, which Breathe renders in "
"`api/cpp.md`. Configuration lives in `docs/Doxyfile`."
msgstr ""

